{
 "opening": "Hey team, here’s the rundown for this release. We’re tackling some key bugs and rolling out new features to make the `parse` library more resilient against tricky data types and edge cases. We’re also adding better ways to inspect results and customize pattern matching.",
 "requirements": [
  {
   "id": "R1",
   "text": "We need a 'letters' format specifier that only matches alphabetic characters. This should be clearly distinct from the 'w' specifier, which includes numbers."
  },
  {
   "id": "R2",
   "text": "Result instances need to implement the `__contains__` method so we can check if a specific value exists in the parsed results."
  },
  {
   "id": "R3",
   "text": "If a part containing braces isn't fully enclosed within matching braces, the Parser must raise an error or fail to match."
  },
  {
   "id": "R4",
   "text": "FixedTzOffset needs to handle timezone offset parsing correctly, addressing the issue outlined in Bug 92."
  },
  {
   "id": "R5",
   "text": "The Parser must be able to correctly parse Fortran-formatted floating-point numbers."
  },
  {
   "id": "R6",
   "text": "The Parser needs to properly identify and convert hexadecimal, binary, and octal integers, supporting optional base arguments as well as automatic base detection."
  },
  {
   "id": "R7",
   "text": "To ensure picklability, the `convert_first` function and its related internal conversion mechanisms must use functors instead of inner functions or lambdas."
  },
  {
   "id": "R8",
   "text": "The `findall` function must respect the `case_sensitive` parameter when searching for patterns."
  },
  {
   "id": "R9",
   "text": "Left- and center-aligned search operations should consume input up to the next space character."
  },
  {
   "id": "R10",
   "text": "Result instances must support slice access so we can retrieve subsets of the parsed values."
  }
 ],
 "closing": "Let's make sure all the public APIs mentioned above behave exactly as described to keep everything compatible and correct."
}
